# oracle: fix nvt/body with pair body/rounded/polyhedron, from examples/body/in.cubes cut down: 2x2x2 replicate of data.cubes (16 cubes), velocity create 1.2 with rot yes, c_n 20, c_t 5, mu 0, A_ua 1, cut 0.5, nvt/body temp 1.2 1.2 0.1, 1000 steps (the example runs 10000). Measured with native LAMMPS (black box): engine vs native max relative error 1.6e-14 (c_p2, step 900) over the thermo rows. The pressure and temperature are read from a separate compute temp/body (tb): a pressure compute on the fix's own temperature compute (1_temp, as in the example) differs from native by 0.2 percent in the kinetic term (measured: native reads the fix temperature before the final thermostat scaling of that step); that is not ported, so the example's compute is replaced.
# oracle-inputs: w121body_cubes_example.data
# oracle-compare: thermo=all atoms=all rel=1e-8 abs=1e-12
units           lj
dimension       3
atom_style      body rounded/polyhedron 1 10
read_data       w121body_cubes_example.data
replicate       2 2 2
velocity        all create 1.2 187287 dist gaussian mom yes rot yes
pair_style      body/rounded/polyhedron 20 5 0 1 0.5
pair_coeff      * * 100 1
comm_modify     vel yes
neighbor        0.5 bin
neigh_modify    every 1 delay 0 check yes
timestep        0.001
fix             1 all nvt/body temp 1.2 1.2 0.1
compute         tb all temp/body
compute         p2 all pressure tb
thermo_style    custom step ke pe etotal c_p2 c_tb
thermo_modify   format float %.15g
thermo          100
run             1000
